  ],
  "This is a contract dispute dressed up as a fraud case.": ["conclusion", "conclusion"],
  "Corvina alleges that a refrigerated trailer failed during a single shipment in August 2025 and that Halvorsen must therefore have lied when it described its “temperature-controlled fleet” months earlier.": [
    "facts",
    "client-fact"
  ],
  "Those allegations do not state a claim for fraud, and they fall well short of the particularity that Rule 9(b) demands.": [
    "conclusion",
    "conclusion"
  ],
  "Nor can Corvina recast a private commercial dispute as a consumer-protection claim under N.Y. Gen. Bus. Law § 349.": [
    "conclusion",
    "conclusion"
  ],
  "The Court should dismiss Counts II and III with prejudice.": ["conclusion", "conclusion"],
  "BACKGROUND": ["heading", "framing"],
  "Corvina distributes fresh seafood to restaurants in the New York metropolitan area. Compl. ¶ 6.": [
    "facts",
    "client-fact"
  ],
  "On March 3, 2025, Corvina and Halvorsen signed a Master Transportation Agreement (the “Agreement”) under which Halvorsen agreed to haul Corvina’s product between Portland, Maine and the Bronx. Id. ¶¶ 12–14; see also Decl. of Tomas Reyes, ECF No. 12, Ex. A.": [
    "facts",
    "client-fact"
  ],
  "The Agreement requires Halvorsen to keep each load between 32 and 38 degrees Fahrenheit and caps Halvorsen’s liability for spoiled cargo at $25,000 per shipment. Agreement §§ 4.2, 9.1.": [
    "facts",
    "client-fact"
  ],
  "According to the Complaint, a Halvorsen sales representative told Corvina’s owner in early 2025 that Halvorsen operated “a fully temperature-controlled fleet with real-time monitoring on every trailer.” (Compl. ¶ 9.)": [
    "facts",
    "client-fact"
  ],
  "On August 14, 2025, a trailer carrying 11,000 pounds of Corvina’s product lost refrigeration near Hartford, Connecticut, and the load spoiled. (Id. ¶¶ 21–23.)": [
    "facts",
    "client-fact"
  ],
  "Corvina alleges that Halvorsen knew some of its older trailers lacked monitoring units. (Id. ¶ 27.)": [
    "facts",
    "client-fact"
